# Men's Round Diamond Ring: 4 Settings That Signal Taste

[![Men's round diamond ring in white gold solitaire — guide to 4 settings that signal taste](/images/mens-round-diamond-ring-featured.jpg "Men's Round Diamond Ring: 4 Settings That Signal Taste — DiamondCritics")](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings?Genders=men&ShapeID=Round&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=Image)

## TL;DR — 4 Settings That Signal Taste

**The setting you choose for a men's round diamond ring signals something specific. Here are the 4 settings and what each one communicates:**

1. **Grooved Solitaire — Restraint:** The band's grooves carry the design. The round stone is an intentional accent. Best for buyers who know less is more.
2. **Ridged/Structured Solitaire — Precision:** Stone and band design are co-equal. The round brilliant reads as a deliberate choice. Best for detail-oriented buyers.
3. **Channel Set — Confidence:** A row of round brilliants sits flush across the band top. The diamond element is primary. Best for buyers comfortable with a clear masculine statement.
4. **Geometric/Statement — Daring:** Round diamonds in a hexagon frame or with brushed-matte contrast. The design leads. Best for fashion-forward buyers.

**All solitaire settings are setting only — add your round brilliant stone separately. Channel rings have diamond weight built in.**

→ Entry pick: **[Tapered Grooved Solitaire, 14k White Gold — $1,000 (sale)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/mens-tapered-grooved-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-item-147386?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)** — most restrained setting; add your round stone separately.

